   "chunk_index": 0,
   "content": "The cell: the unit of life\n\nWhat is a cell?\n\nThe cell is the smallest living unit of a living thing. Every living thing is made\nof one cell or of many cells. The human body has a huge number of cells\nthat work together.\n\nMost cells are very small. We need a microscope to see them.\n\nThe main parts of a cell\n\nMost cells have three main parts: the cell membrane, the cytoplasm and the\nnucleus.\n\nThe cell membrane\n\nThe cell membrane is a thin cover around the cell. It lets in what the cell\nneeds, such as water and food. It lets waste out. So the membrane controls\nwhat enters the cell and what leaves it.\n\nThe cytoplasm\n\nThe cytoplasm is a jelly-like material that fills the cell. Small parts called\norganelles float in it.\n\n\fThe nucleus\n\nThe nucleus is the control centre of the cell. It keeps the genetic material,\nwhich carries the instructions for the traits of the living thing. The nucleus\ndirects the work of the cell, such as growth and division.\n\nThe mitochondria\n\nMitochondria are small organelles in the cytoplasm. Their job is to produce\nthe energy the cell needs. They take in food and oxygen, and they turn the\nenergy stored in food into energy the cell can use. This process is called\ncellular respiration. That is why mitochondria are called the powerhouse of\nthe cell.\n\nCells that do a lot of work need more energy. So muscle cells have many\nmitochondria.\n\nPlant cells and animal cells\n\nBoth have a membrane, cytoplasm, a nucleus and mitochondria. A plant cell\nhas some extra parts:\n\n- The cell wall: a stiff wall outside the membrane. It supports the cell and\ngives it its shape.\n\n- Chloroplasts: they make food from sunlight, water and carbon dioxide. This\nis photosynthesis.\n\n- A large vacuole: it stores water.\n\nSummary\n\nThe cell is the unit of life. The membrane controls what goes in and out. The\nnucleus keeps the genetic material. The mitochondria produce energy. A\nplant cell also has a cell wall, chloroplasts and a large vacuole.\n\n",
